From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] journal: report result-set readiness failures

The GTK4 Journal must not silently leave a blank canvas when the datastore
result-set callback fails. Log the failing operation with a traceback so the
runtime owner is observable while preserving the existing error semantics.

--- a/src/jarabe/journal/listmodel.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/journal/listmodel.py
@@ -108,5 +108,9 @@ class ListModel(GObject.GObject, Gtk.TreeModel):
     def __result_set_ready_cb(self, **kwargs):
         t = time.time()
-        self._all_ids = self._result_set.find_ids(self._query)
+        try:
+            self._all_ids = self._result_set.find_ids(self._query)
+        except Exception:
+            logging.exception('Journal result-set readiness failed')
+            raise
         logging.debug('get all ids: %r', time.time() - t)
         self.emit('ready')
